       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
       │                                               │
 [ SECTOR-01: X-RAD ]                            [ SECTOR-02: X-IR ]
Spatial Cross-Radiometry                        Thermal & Optical Drift
 (Kinematic Echoes)                              (Persistent Signatures)
       │                                               │
       └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘
                               │
       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐
       │                                               │
 [ SECTOR-03: X-SPEC ]                           [ SECTOR-04: X-NET ]
EM Spectrum Coherence                           Cyber Layer Attestation
 (Jamming/Null Floor)                            (Identity Overlays)

```
## 🔄 2. The MDC Ghost Correlation Matrix
When an anomalous signature hits the X-FIR array, it is parsed through the 6-axis MDC tensor to determine whether it is hardware, software, or an electronic phantom.
| X-FIR Sector Trigger | Dimensional Anomaly Detected | System State Classification |
|---|---|---|
| **X-RAD (Kinematic)** | Mass/Velocity signature without an active Flight Corridor (W-MC) entry. | **Stealth Physical Incursion** |
| **X-IR (Thermal)** | Thermal bloom matching active propulsion, but reporting zero RF emissions. | **Silent Orbit Maneuver** |
| **X-SPEC (Spectrum)** | Localized noise floor drop or micro-dazzling event on communications link. | **Active EM Spoofing / Jamming** |
| **X-NET (Cyber)** | Valid data packets arriving from a ground telemetry route with stale timestamps. | **Replay Attack / Zero-Day Vector** |
## 🛠️ 3. Deploying the X-FIR Ghost Hunting Nodule
Instruct Manus to integrate this operational module into the active background runner as xfir-ghost-detector.js. This script cross-evaluates incoming sector data streams, isolates uncorrelated anomalies, and passes their dimensional coordinates straight to the *ThreatGraph* for automated neutralization.
